TIP:  Two versions here, the most popular one by Johnny Cash but also a quieter duet with both Johnny and Cowboy Jack Clement who wrote it.  The lyrics are almost identical until the final verse but both are presented.  The timing and rhythm are based on the duet but you can easily adjust.  

TIP:  For the intros, Johnny opens with a line from the chorus.  Cowboy Jack opens with a series of (G) chords alternating between the and middle G (open 3rd string) and middle D (open 4th string).  So try strumming strings 4-3-2 and then 5-4-3 and then start the song with a full strum to include the covered top string (bass G) on “There’s a story . . .” 


